        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Service Definition From Document"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774802097402"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_SERVICE_DEFINITION_FROM_DOCUMENT",
          "id": "1774802063733",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774802063735_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are extracting a digital government service definition from a physical document and returning API-ready JSON for service setup creation.\n\nGoal:\nFrom the provided form text and reference data, extract:\n1) the service definition for:\n   POST /api/boss/data/objects/ora/digitalGovCore/setup/v1/services\n2) the service characteristics for:\n   POST /api/boss/data/objects/ora/digitalGovCore/setup/v1/services/{services_id}/serviceCharacteristics\n   (one payload per characteristic)\n\nInput:\n- Form Text: {{raw_text}}\n- Physical Document Context: {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_UPLOADED_DOCUMENTS.$output}}\n- Categories Reference JSON: {{$context.$nodes.RETRIEVE_SERVICE_CATEGORIES.$output}}\n- Business Units Reference JSON: {{$context.$nodes.RETRIEVE_BUSINESS_UNITS.$output}}\n- Lookups Reference JSON (Type): {{$context.$nodes.RETRIEVE_SERVICE_TYPE_LOOKUPS.$output}}\n\nRequired resolution flow before building payloads:\n1) Determine the best matching Business Unit from the provided Business Units reference.\n2) Determine the best matching Category from the provided Categories reference, limited to the selected Business Unit when applicable.\n3) Determine the best matching Service Type from the provided Type Lookups reference.\n\nGeneral rules:\n- Return only one valid JSON object.\n- Do not include markdown, commentary, or trailing commas.\n- Do not invent IDs, lookup codes, or values not supported by the provided inputs.\n- If a value cannot be confidently determined, set it to null.\n- Prefer exact or near-exact matches from the provided reference JSON inputs.\n- Keep only fields that are needed; do not include unknown or unsupported fields.\n\nService extraction rules:\n- name:\n  - Required.\n  - Convert the document title into a safe system identifier.\n  - Use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE consistently.\n  - Replace spaces and punctuation with underscores.\n  - Collapse multiple underscores.\n  - Remove leading/trailing underscores.\n- displayName:\n  - Required.\n  - Human-readable title case.\n- description:\n  - Required.\n  - Brief purpose statement based on the document.\n  - If not explicitly present, summarize only if clearly inferable.\n- internalRecordFlag:\n  - Set to true unless the document explicitly indicates it is external.\n  - If unclear, default to true.\n- businessUnit.id:\n  - Required.\n  - Select the single best business unit from the Business Units reference JSON.\n  - Prefer exact/near-exact match to names mentioned in the document header, department, or program.\n  - If no match is found, use 204.\n- type.lookupCode:\n  - Required.\n  - Select the single best lookup code from the Type Lookups reference JSON.\n  - Prefer exact/near-exact match.\n  - If no match is found, use ORA_DGV_CERTIFICATE.\n- category.id:\n  - Required.\n  - Select the single best category from the Categories reference JSON.\n  - Prefer exact/near-exact match.\n  - If multiple are plausible and cannot be disambiguated, use the category whose name is exactly \"Life Events\" if present.\n  - Otherwise choose the closest match.\n\nAdditional fields extraction rules:\n- Extract every fillable field needed to digitize the form.\n- Include:\n  - text blanks\n  - labeled lines\n  - colon fields\n  - checkboxes, yes/no, radio selections\n  - dates, amounts, counts, IDs\n  - signatures, printed name, and signature date as separate fields\n  - addresses split into separate lines if the form implies it\n- Do not include:\n  - section headers with no input\n  - boilerplate legal text unless it creates an explicit field\n  - duplicate repeats unless needed; if repeated, disambiguate with a suffix such as managerSignature or employeeSignature\n\nField rules for each additional field:\n- fieldName:\n  - Required.\n  - Unique, concise camelCase.\n- fieldDisplayName:\n  - Required.\n  - Exact label text as it appears after removing leading numeral/letter/bullet artifacts such as:\n    1., 1), (1), 1-, 1:, a., A), (b), I., ii), •, -, –, —, *, ►, ▪\n  - Trim the result.\n- fieldDataType:\n  - Required.\n  - Use one of: STRING, NUMBER, DATE, TIMESTAMP, BOOLEAN.\n\nOutput schema:\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"displayName\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"internalRecordFlag\": true,\n  \"businessUnit\": {\n    \"id\": null\n  },\n  \"type\": {\n    \"lookupCode\": null\n  },\n  \"category\": {\n    \"id\": null\n  },\n  \"additionalFields\": [\n    {\n      \"fieldName\": \"\",\n      \"fieldDisplayName\": \"\",\n      \"fieldDataType\": \"\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nReturn only the JSON object."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Validate Service Creation Payload"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774802132429"
          },
          "code": "VALIDATE_SERVICE_CREATION_PAYLOAD",
          "id": "1774802097402",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774802097403_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "System / Instruction:\nYou are a workflow debug step in Oracle AI Agent Studio. Return ONLY valid JSON. Do not include markdown or commentary. Your job is to output the resolved Create Service payload exactly as it should be sent to the Business Object POST call.\n\nTask:\nUsing the values from {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SERVICE_DEFINITION_FROM_DOCUMENT.$output}}, produce the JSON payload for “Create Services” with this structure:\n\n{\n\"name\": <name>,\n\"displayName\": <displayName>,\n\"description\": <description>,\n\"internalRecordFlag\": <internalRecordFlag>,\n\"businessUnit\": { \"id\": <businessUnitId> },\n\"type\": { \"lookupCode\": <lookupCode> },\n\"category\": { \"id\": <categoryId> }\n}\n\nRules:\n\nOutput ONLY the JSON payload (single JSON object).\nPreserve correct JSON types:\ninternalRecordFlag must be boolean (true/false), not a string.\nbusinessUnit.id and category.id must be numbers if the input values are numbers.\nIf any required value is missing, set it to null (do not guess).\nInput values:\nname = {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SERVICE_DEFINITION_FROM_DOCUMENT.$output.name}}  \ndisplayName = {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SERVICE_DEFINITION_FROM_DOCUMENT.$output.displayName}}\ndescription = {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SERVICE_DEFINITION_FROM_DOCUMENT.$output.description}}\ninternalRecordFlag = {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SERVICE_DEFINITION_FROM_DOCUMENT.$output.internalRecordFlag}}\nbusinessUnitId = {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SERVICE_DEFINITION_FROM_DOCUMENT.$output.businessUnit.id}}\nlookupCode = {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SERVICE_DEFINITION_FROM_DOCUMENT.$output.type.lookupCode}}\ncategoryId = {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SERVICE_DEFINITION_FROM_DOCUMENT.$output.category.id}}\n\nReturn the final JSON now."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_COM_OTHER_SERVICES",
